abstract: >
  NRA-IDE is a structural boundary-evaluation framework in which
  Cause-Side observations and rules fixed before evaluation determine
  accumulated deviation delta, absorption thickness tau, and the canonical
  boundary-approach ratio R = delta / tau. A higher R indicates closer
  approach to structural rupture. The framework distinguishes boundary
  warning, human handoff, irreversible-transition onset, and the invariant
  complete-rupture boundary at R = 1.0. It prohibits Effect-Side outputs
  from updating delta, tau, or R. NRA-IDE is not a PID variant; tau is not
  a time constant, and R is not a safety, confidence, or quality score.